      "title": "Sound Designer/ Mentor (PT Paid Per Production)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\n\nLocation: Grand Rapids\n\nThe AQ Theatre Program Sound Designer/Mentor will be responsible for: Sound design for one or more of the mainstage theatre productions Working with the Director of the production on sound concept Attending all production meetings Attending a designer run-through during the rehearsal process Providing updates on the sound design, as requested by the Director and/or the Theatre Program Director Having all sound effects entered before the technical rehearsal Attending the technical rehearsal(s) Mentoring one or more students on sound design and sound board functioning Participating in the production strike, as needed Mic actors as requested by the Director/Technical Director/Musical Director, Theatre Program Director, Working with the Musical Director (when applicable) to achieve sound balance, Reporting any concerns with sound board/microphone functioning to the Technical Director (Kelsey Edwards) Report to the Theatre Program Director (Dr. Penny Avery).",
